<speak>
<s>This is your Jumu'ah briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">17072026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>The United States has widened its war on Iran from weapons sites to the roads and rails that civilians use, striking five bridges near Bandar Abbas and killing at least three people.</s> <s>Marines are now boarding tankers under a naval blockade begun this week, turning the Strait of Hormuz into contested water where any ship is a potential target.</s> <s>Tehran, in turn, has asked Yemen's Houthis to stand ready to close the Red Sea.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Nicaragua has severed diplomatic relations with Italy over a killing that happened forty-eight years ago.</s> <s>Managua has sheltered Alessio Casimirri, convicted in the murder of former premier Aldo Moro, since nineteen eighty-three, and its constitution forbids extraditing its own citizens.</s> <s>Rome keeps demanding his return, and a Cold War-era act of political violence has now ruptured two states.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Damascus, post-Assad Syria's attempt to reckon with an old atrocity may be sweeping up the innocent.</s> <s>A war-crimes case tied to the twenty thirteen Tadamon massacre appears, on close reporting, to rest on false evidence, even as the new government arrests alleged perpetrators.</s> <s>Transitional justice depends on getting the facts right, and the hardest problem isn't the guilty but the wrongly accused.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Gaza's reconstruction plan has shrunk to a single pilot camp.</s> <s>The board overseeing recovery admits only limited progress, fearing that visible failure would strengthen Israeli factions pushing to transfer the population out.</s> <s>Little of the pledged seventeen billion dollars has materialized, and no construction has yet begun.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Dhaka, the young people who toppled a government two years ago are back on the streets.</s> <s>The same Gen Z cohort behind the twenty twenty-four uprising is mobilizing again, this time over disputed grading in the country's Higher Secondary Certificate exams.</s> <s>Interim authorities haven't said whether they'll revise the results, and a movement that once removed a prime minister is testing its power again.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>New Zealand has signed a new trade pact with India, a deliberate turn away from its heavy dependence on China.</s> <s>For a small Pacific economy the deal is less about tariffs than about hedging its bets, and India is fast becoming the destination for nations trying to de-risk from Beijing.</s> <s>Exporters now wait on the fine print — the tariff schedule and market access terms still to come.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The ratings agency S&P forecasts credit growth of five to six percent for Gulf banks this year, even as war rattles their neighborhood.</s> <s>Project finance and consumer lending keep expanding while tension over Hormuz threatens the very shipping lanes these economies sit on.</s> <s>That forecast is really a bet — that the war stays offshore of Gulf balance sheets.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Uber is buying Berlin's Delivery Hero in a deal that values the German company at fourteen point eight billion dollars.</s> <s>Food delivery is a scale-or-die business, and this folds one of the last independent global players into an American giant, from Europe to the Gulf, where Delivery Hero owns Talabat.</s> <s>Regulators must still clear the merger, which wouldn't close until the second half of twenty twenty-seven.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nigeria's central bank will now track every single purchase of foreign currency at the country's exchange bureaus.</s> <s>It's banning exclusivity deals and referral fees between banks and bureaus, an attempt to break the cartels that ration access to dollars.</s> <s>Bureaus that hoard unsold currency face fines or suspension from the market.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A fresh look at five royal mummies suggests some ancient Egyptian princesses were trained fighters, not merely buried with ceremonial weapons.</s> <s>Researchers found forearm and hand bones bowed and thickened in ways consistent with regular use of the bow and dagger around three thousand eight hundred years ago.</s> <s>Other scientists caution the same changes could come from unrelated labor, so the debate over these women's lives isn't settled.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In the Democratic Republic of Congo, an Ebola outbreak has now killed seven hundred ninety-six people and is spreading nearly five times faster than the outbreak of twenty eighteen.</s> <s>The <sub alias="World Health Organization">WHO</sub> says the virus reached two thousand cases in just two months.</s> <s>More troubling, over eighty percent of new cases appear outside known contact lists, meaning the chains of transmission are being missed.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Astronomers have found a detectable atmosphere on a rocky world in its star's habitable zone, a first of its kind.</s> <s>They detected helium around the planet known as <sub alias="L H S eleven forty b">LHS 1140-b</sub> — hydrogen escapes such worlds easily, but helium lingers, proving a small rocky planet can hold onto an atmosphere.</s> <s>Follow-up observations will now search that air for any sign of life, God willing.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>China's Moonshot AI has released the first open model to reach two point eight trillion parameters, a scale until now locked inside closed American labs.</s> <s>Called Kimi K three, its full weights are due for public release by the twenty-seventh of July, letting anyone download capability that US firms have kept behind paywalls.</s> <s>The move pressures those closed labs on both price and secrecy.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Russia's elite military hackers, the group known as Sandworm, have adopted a trick borrowed from ordinary online scams.</s> <s>They compromised Ukrainian networks with a fake security check that fools victims into pasting malicious commands themselves — a technique migrating from petty crime into state espionage.</s> <s>Ukraine's emergency response team is urging administrators to lock their systems down.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A United States senator is warning that Canada's proposed surveillance law would weaken security for people far beyond its borders.</s> <s>Ron Wyden says the lawful-access bill would force tech firms to hand over data and build backdoors, and because that infrastructure is shared, the damage wouldn't stop at Canada's edge.</s> <s>His letter asks Washington to press Ottawa, turning a domestic bill into a global privacy fight.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Taiwan's <sub alias="T S M C">TSMC</sub>, the world's leading chipmaker, saw its stock fall even as profit jumped seventy-seven percent.</s> <s>Tariff pressure from Washington pushed the company to raise its total investment in Arizona to two hundred sixty-five billion dollars.</s> <s>Yet its chief executive gave no timeline for construction, saying the pace depends on the market.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>